{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "dayofweek_itp_NOx",
    "description": "NEI 2016 day-of-week emission scale factor for NOx. Weekday=high, weekend=low.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "nei2016",
      "emissions",
      "nox",
      "dayofweek",
      "registered_function"
    ],
    "created": "2026-05-30T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciData.jl contributors",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-8p6a)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a:src/nei2016monthly.jl:112."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "dayofweek_itp_NOx": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a:src/nei2016monthly.jl:112\nFactors: [1.0706, 1.0706, 1.0706, 1.0706, 1.0706, 0.863, 0.784]\nday_of_week (1=Mon, 7=Sun) = (D+3) mod 7 + 1\n  where D = floor(t_local/86400), t_local = t_utc + floor(lon*180/(pi*15))*3600\nNote: Test timestamps use positive values (>= epoch) to avoid float rounding\nissue where 1/86400 coefficient causes floor error for negative timestamps.\n\nUpdated 2026-10-28 to EarthSciML/EarthSciData.jl PR #226 (head jialinl6:Oct_merge @87f8da1): the local time uses round(lon/15) with ties to even, the EDGAR NOx hourly clock GEOS-Chem uses, instead of floor(lon/15). Expected values are upstream's function at each test's inputs."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-10
      },
      "variables": {
        "t_utc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "UTC time as seconds since Unix epoch (1970-01-01T00:00:00Z = Thursday)."
        },
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude in radians. Used to compute local solar time."
        },
        "dayofweek_itp_NOx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "NEI 2016 day-of-week emission scale factor for NOx. Weekday=high, weekend=low. (dimensionless scale factor)."
        }
      },
